      "writtenOn": "2025-06-20T14:57:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For nonlinear SKBs, the only thing stored in the SKB (as opposed to being stored in fragment pages) is the virtio header. `skb-\u003etail` is updated to reflect that in `virtio_vsock_alloc_skb_with_frags()`, thanks to the call to `skb_reserve(skb, VIRTIO_VSOCK_SKB_HEADROOM)`.\n\nSo I don\u0027t think `skb-\u003etail` requires further adjustment here.",
      "parentUuid": "1e6c8576_80070a3f",
      "revId": "8ba8cdb0fc03e5a0b1d09b24896aafa8eab93da0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
